WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.610
Local LLM infrastructure is a systems-engineering problem.

00:00:04.690 --> 00:00:17.367
It combines CPU, GPU, VRAM or unified memory, system RAM, storage, power, cooling, operating system, drivers, runtime, model, interfaces, security, and maintenance.

00:00:17.447 --> 00:00:25.515
Local and cloud inference offer different control, capability, cost, scaling, privacy, and operational tradeoffs.

00:00:25.595 --> 00:00:30.205
Choose according to measured requirements rather than ideology.

00:00:30.285 --> 00:00:37.776
Model fit depends on parameters, architecture, quantization, context, cache, concurrency, offload, and overhead.

00:00:37.856 --> 00:00:45.347
A model that loads is not necessarily stable or useful under real demand.

00:00:45.427 --> 00:00:55.224
Start with a simple supported stack, trusted model source, known configuration, representative benchmark, and clear acceptance criteria.

00:00:55.304 --> 00:01:01.066
Measure prompt processing, generation, latency, quality, memory, thermals, and failures.

00:01:01.146 --> 00:01:08.061
Protect APIs, accounts, networks, prompts, documents, logs, backups, and model supply chains.

00:01:08.141 --> 00:01:14.480
Scale only when a real workload justifies more hardware or orchestration.

00:01:14.560 --> 00:01:20.322
Strong local systems are maintainable, secure, measured, and appropriately modest.
